                "event": "Flood Watch",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Miami FL",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 19 at 3:18PM EST until November 20 at 7:00AM EST by NWS Miami FL",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southeast Florida, including the following\nareas, Coastal Broward County, Coastal Miami Dade County, Coastal\nPalm Beach County, Far South Miami-Dade County, Inland Broward\nCounty, Inland Miami-Dade County, Inland Palm Beach County, Metro\nBroward County, Metro Palm Beach County and Metropolitan Miami\nDade.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Widespread 3 to 5 inches of rain have fallen across the east\ncoast of South Florida over the past several days, with pockets\nof 8 to 15 inches. Areas having received these higher end amounts\nare most susceptible to today's forecast rain amounts. Common\nrainfall amounts in locations impacted by showers for the rest of\nthe afternoon and into tonight will be 1 to 2 inches, with the\nisolated high end amounts closer to 3 to 5 inches.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFAMFL"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS62 KMFL 192018"
                    ],
                    "NWSheadline": [
