                "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 19 at 6:29AM AKST until November 19 at 6:00PM AKST by NWS Anchorage AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Small stream and localized urban flooding caused by\nexcessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Including the following area, Southern Kenai Mtns. This\nincludes the city of Seward.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM AKST this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nStorm drains and ditches may become clogged with debris. Flooding\nmay occur in poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Rainfall is still on track to decrease late this afternoon.\nProlonged heavy rain may lead to areas of flooding along smaller\nstreams and creeks, in low-lying and poor drainage areas, and\nponding of water on roadways.\n\n- Http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.\n\nYou should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
