                "senderName": "NWS Jacksonville FL",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 19 at 9:10AM EST until November 20 at 7:00PM EST by NWS Jacksonville FL",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northeast Florida, including the following\nareas, Coastal Duval, Coastal Flagler, Eastern Clay, Eastern\nPutnam, Inland Flagler, Northeast Coastal St. Johns, Northern\nInland St. Johns, South Central Duval, Southeast Coastal St. Johns,\nSouthern Inland St. Johns, Trout River, Western Clay, Western\nDuval, Western Putnam and Western St. Johns.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Several rounds of heavy rainfall are expected to repeatedly occur\nin the watch area through at least early Friday evening. Repeated\nrounds of heavy rainfall will result in the potential for urban\nand small    stream flooding across portions of northeast and\nnorth central Florida. Widespread rainfall totals of 3 to 6\ninches are forecast, with locally higher amounts up to 12 inches\npossible.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
